From: WFI-030 rows two and three — frozen-artifact Done When detection
Subject: [PATCH] feat(review-loop): record Done When items naming a frozen artifact

Human-applied patch. All three files are protected role or gate artifacts (the
two precheck twins become protected once WFI-037 step (a) lands), so an agent
may stage this diff but may not apply it.
See docs/workflow-improvements/WFI-030.md.

Apply with:
    git apply reports/notes/wfi-030b-frozen-done-when-detection.patch

Companion to reports/notes/wfi-030-traceability-status-normalization.patch,
which covers row one. The two are independent and may be applied in either
order.

DETECTION ONLY. The precheck exit code is unchanged by a non-empty
frozen_artifact_done_when array. Measured over all 34 task plans in this
repository the trigger fires on 6 items, 3 of them real:

  sdd-domain-concept-contract  T-002:289  T-003:412  T-004:529   real
  epic-136-phase3              T-001:363                        false positive
  epic-136-phase4-mcp          T-004:1224                       false positive
  sdd-domain                   T-006:542                        false positive

The false positives cite a frozen filename parenthetically next to an unrelated
write verb. They are the same grammatical shape as the real items, so a hard
precheck failure at 3-in-6 would block half the plans it fires on. Adjudication
moves to the review gate instead.

A line-at-a-time scan finds only 1 of the 3 real items: T-003 and T-004 wrap
across a continuation line, putting the artifact name and the verb on different
lines. Both twins join continuation lines before matching.

Verification performed: the scan reproduces exactly the 6 rows above, with
correct task IDs and first-line numbers, over specs/*/tasks.md. The twin-parity
and fixture tests of WFI-030's Verification Plan items 5-8 are NOT yet written.
Do not treat this patch as verified until they run.

--- a/plugins/sdd-review-loop/scripts/task-review-precheck.sh
+++ b/plugins/sdd-review-loop/scripts/task-review-precheck.sh
@@ -355,6 +355,40 @@
 fi
 
 [[ "${workflow_match_precheck}" != "FAIL" ]] || fail "Risk/Required Workflow mismatches must be fixed before creating evidence"
+
+# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# STEP 2b: Record Done When items that name a review-frozen artifact (WFI-030)
+# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Detection only -- this never changes the exit code. The frozen-artifact rule
+# in the task decomposition review gate's structural-coverage role is a Major
+# finding evaluated by reviewer judgement alone; nothing deterministic backed
+# it, and a review that reasoned past it sealed an unsatisfiable item into a
+# hash-bound plan. Measured over this repository the trigger fires on 6 items,
+# 3 of them real, so it records rather than fails; the reviewer adjudicates
+# each entry.
+# Items wrap across continuation lines, so lines are joined into whole items
+# before matching: a line-at-a-time scan finds only 1 of the 3 known cases.
+frozen_done_when_tsv="$(awk '
+  function flush(   l) {
+    if (item == "") return
+    l = item
+    if (l ~ /traceability\.md|design\.md|tasks\.md/ &&
+        l ~ /(^|[^a-zA-Z])(record|records|update|updates|add|write|edit|append)([^a-zA-Z]|$)/)
+      printf "%s\t%d\t%s\n", task, itemline, l
+    item = ""
+  }
+  /^##[ \t]+T-[0-9]+/ { flush(); task = $2; sub(/[^A-Za-z0-9-].*$/, "", task); inblk = 0 }
+  /Done When/ { flush(); inblk = 1; next }
+  /^(##|###)[ \t]/ || /^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z ]*:/ { flush(); inblk = 0 }
+  !inblk { next }
+  /^- \[/ { flush(); item = $0; itemline = FNR; next }
+  /^[ \t]+[^ \t]/ { if (item != "") { sub(/^[ \t]+/, " "); item = item $0 }; next }
+  { flush() }
+  END { flush() }
+' "${TASKS_MD}")"
+frozen_done_when_json="$(printf '%s' "${frozen_done_when_tsv}" |
+  jq -R -s -c 'split("\n") | map(select(length > 0) | split("\t") | {task: .[0], line: (.[1]|tonumber), item: .[2]})')"
+[[ -n "${frozen_done_when_json}" ]] || frozen_done_when_json='[]'
 
 # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 # STEP 3: Parse Blockers fields and build dependency-graph.json
@@ -620,6 +652,7 @@
   "acceptance_sha256": "${acceptance_sha256}",
   "design_sha256": "${design_sha256}",
   "traceability_sha256": "${traceability_sha256}",
+  "frozen_artifact_done_when": ${frozen_done_when_json},
   "layer_sha256": ${layer_sha256},
   "input_sha256": "${input_sha256}",
   "generated_at": "${generated_at}"
